00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:53.960
Now here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:56.120
Want to know a secret about Сонсо?

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:04.820
The Russian word «сонсо» and the English word «солар» are actually cousins from the exact same ancient root.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:09.300
They both come from a very old word that meant «сон».

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:15.580
This word travelled through Latin as «сол», which gave us «солар», «соларь» and even «сон».

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:19.040
In Slavic languages, it became «сонсо».

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.920
Along the way, the word picked up an «н» sound in Russian.

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:27.420
«Сол» и «с» — but the family connection is still there.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:28.720
Here is a fun gocha.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:34.920
The Russian word for «сон» flower is «потсолну», which literally means «under the sun».

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:41.780
So next time you see a «сон» flower or hear the word «солар», remember it is cousins with «сонсо».

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:48.340
That hidden family link is your secret shortcut to remembering the Russian word forever.

